Z||000000||Lou Christopher||06-19-2001||08:46 AM||||I have an 85 Se with a 350 chev. Want to add aux gauges on top of the center console.  I recently bought a set of gauges and pod enclosure on E bay. It came with a metl mounting bracket under the pod.  Obviously I can not install it this way on the console.  how does it mount? do I cut away the top of the console to recess the mount? Help. I am installing digital H2o and oil pressure gauges in the pod so if anyone wants just the gauges let me know.<BR>                  Lou Christopher||||reg||5
Z||000001||fieroluke||06-19-2001||10:06 AM||||Hi Lou,<P>maybe I can earn the gauge guts by helping you out ;-)<P><BR>I installed the gauges on my 85GT, and the modification was not that difficult.<P>You have to remove the shifter knob, shifter console, radio fascia and radio surround pod.<P>Now you should be able to see a metal support connecting the dash to the center console support.<BR>This metal thing needs to have holes drilled into it. Set the aux gauge housing on top of the dash<BR>(where it's supposed to be). You probably have to remove two nuts to hold it against the support flush.<BR>Anyway, the top two holes should line up, nor mark the bottom two holes, remove the metal support<BR>and drill holes there. When installing, no need to drill holes into the dash behind the support, it's<BR>plastic/foam, the screws tap themselves. Before you do that though, cut a small, 1" wide, 1/2" long<BR>oval hole into the dash to feed the wires through. Even with your digital gauges, the wires need to go somewhere.<BR>Fiddling the wires through there may be a hassle, but that's it.<P>I recommend getting a new radio surround with the opening on top for the extra gauges, but you can<BR>also cut a hole in the old console support. That's up to you...<P>Best regards,<P>-Oliver<BR>||||reg||12
Z||000002||Lou Christopher||06-19-2001||11:23 AM||||Oliver,  You are welcome to the gauges for whatever shipping costs.  If i understand you properly when I take the radio surround off I will find a matting piece for the bracket that is on the bottom of my gauges.  dril a coulple holes, open up back of dash for wires. Question if I have to cut the radio surround to get it over the aux pod how do I obtain a finished look.  Or am I missing something.<BR>                Lou||||reg||1
